/*
Problem: N-Repeated Element in Size 2N Array (LC 961)
Topic: Sorting

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

Sort the array so that equal elements
become adjacent.

The element repeated N times will
appear consecutively after sorting.

Traverse the sorted array and return
the first adjacent duplicate.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. Sort the array.

2. Traverse from index 1.

3. If the current element equals the
   previous element:

   Return that element.

4. (This case never occurs according
   to the problem constraints.)

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

[1,2,3,3]

Sorted:

[1,2,3,3]

Adjacent duplicate:

3

Answer:

3

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

[5,1,5,2]

Sorted:

[1,2,5,5]

Adjacent duplicate:

5

Answer:

5

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

Sorting groups identical elements
together.

Since one element appears exactly N
times, it must have at least one
adjacent duplicate after sorting.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n log n)

Sorting dominates the complexity.

Space : O(1)

Ignoring the space used internally by
the sorting algorithm.

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

Sorting
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int repeatedNTimes(vector<int>& nums) {

        // Sort the array
        sort(nums.begin(), nums.end());

        // Find adjacent duplicate
        for (int i = 1;
             i < nums.size();
             i++) {

            if (nums[i] == nums[i - 1])
                return nums[i];
        }

        return 0;
    }
};
